     ---
     Smart Proxy Evaluation & Corrections

     Phase 1 — HFS In-Memory Check ✓ (correct, with additions)

     - Normalise query before lookup: lowercase, trim, collapse whitespace.
     - Trie gives O(k) prefix lookup (k = query length), easily handles 1,000 entries.
     - Addition: Skip Azure entirely if query is < 3 characters; return HFS prefix matches only.

     Phase 2 — Intent Detection ✓ (correct, with refinements)

     - Question heuristic: leading question words (how, what, where, when, why, can i, do i, is there, am i) or trailing ?.
     - Correction: Add word-count threshold — queries > 4 words are treated as questions even without question words (conversational phrasing).
     - This whole phase is a regex + word-count check, < 0.1 ms.

     Phase 3 — Azure AI Search ⚠️ (corrections required)

     - Keyword path: Azure Suggesters only do exact prefix match. Replace with search=*&queryType=full&$search={q}~1 (fuzzy, edit distance 1) for better recall at acceptable speed.
     - Question path: Semantic Answers adds ~20–50 ms. This is acceptable if Azure responds within ~75 ms total.
     - New: Circuit Breaker — if Azure does not respond within 80 ms, abort and return the best available HFS partial matches. Protects the SLA.
     - New: Parallel execution — for ambiguous intent (no clear question/keyword signal), fire both paths concurrently and merge; take the first response that returns.

